---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/layout/BaseLayout.astro';
import PagedShelf from '../../components/review/PagedShelf.astro';
import {getShelfCatalog} from '../../lib/shelf-catalog';
import operations from '../../data/phase-207-current-operations.json';
import ledger from '../../data/phase-206-editorial-classification.json';
import adjudications from '../../data/owner-authorized-adjudications.json';
import reviews from '../../data/selected-article-ai-reviews.json';
import {translatedReaders} from '../../lib/translated-readers.mjs';
import {annualAiReviewData,annualAiDecisions} from '../../lib/annual-ai-reviews.mjs';
const {classification}=await getShelfCatalog();
---
<BaseLayout title="Editorial classification review | FTFN">
  <section class="page-section" data-review-policy={adjudications.policy_id}>
    <h1 class="page-title">Editorial review and decisions</h1>
    <h2>Owner-authorized AI review · {adjudications.decision_date}</h2>
    <p>The owner has authorized Codex to make editorial, eligibility, backlog and language determinations. Human sign-off is not a build prerequisite. Each determination identifies its evidence and limits; historical human-review fields are not rewritten as approvals.</p>
    <p>This does not authorize publication, claim a human reader study, or create missing operating measurements. <a href="/data/current-operations.json">Review policy, research receipts and backlog decisions</a>.</p>
    <p><a href="/method/portfolio-decisions/">103 portfolio identity and counting determinations</a> · <a href="/atlas/projects/montana-bead/">32 Montana project dossiers</a>. French uses fr-CA; Spanish uses es-419. <a href="/reference/accessible-editions/">{translatedReaders.length} of 34 complete translated readings</a> use the later plain-language English text. {translatedReaders.length===34?'All seventeen topics now have both local language editions. These are AI-authored and AI-reviewed readings, not independent human assessments, accessibility certification or fresh source inspections.':'The remaining texts still need completion and AI review.'}</p>
  </section>
  <section class="page-section" data-selected-review-index>
    <h2>{reviews.reviewed_articles} of {reviews.selected_article_target} selected articles assessed by AI</h2>
    <p>These exact-version decisions were made {reviews.decision_date}. All {reviews.selected_article_target} selected articles now carry their decisions and required corrections. All {annualAiReviewData.reviewed_annual_records} annual assessments are integrated below; wider reachable-content review remains separate work. A decision accepts a bounded editorial treatment, not every linked claim or a newly verified operating result. Complete original paragraphs and earlier human-review fields remain history.</p>
    <ul>{reviews.records.map(r=><li><a href={`${r.route}#${r.record_id}-ai-review`}>{r.title}</a> — {r.decision}</li>)}</ul>
    <p><a href="/data/build-decisions.json">Exact decisions, located findings and input hashes</a></p>
  </section>
  <section class="page-section" data-annual-ai-index>
    <h2>{annualAiReviewData.reviewed_annual_records} of {annualAiReviewData.annual_target} annual records assessed by AI</h2>
    <p>All 58 annual records are assessed: 24 case profiles, 17 topic chapters, 12 syntheses and five appendices. The twelve paired essay presentations have their own exact input bindings; they do not add annual records. Across 70 readings, 66 paragraph corrections preserve their earlier wording. The final 24 decisions were assessed September 27 and integrated September 29, adding 32 corrections without a new primary inspection. The earlier AEMO, FAA and NOAA checks retain their recorded scope and dates. Translations, wider content, measurement evidence and release acceptance remain separate.</p>
    {annualAiDecisions.map(decision=><section id={`${decision.record_id}-annual-decision`}><h3>{decision.record_id}: {decision.disposition.replaceAll('_',' ')}</h3><p>{decision.rationale}</p><ul>{decision.readings.map((reading:{route:string;record_id:string})=><li><a href={`${reading.route}#${reading.record_id}-ai-review`}>{reading.record_id}: current reading and AI assessment</a></li>)}</ul></section>)}
    <p><a href="/data/build-decisions.json">Exact annual decisions, source checks and input hashes</a>. Source-check dates remain separate from article review dates; no human study, new operating outcome or release is implied.</p>
  </section>
  <section class="page-section">
    <h2>Internal tests are not external operating results.</h2>
    <p class="lede">{ledger.individually_reviewed} individual classifications are recorded, including {ledger.corrected_presentations} corrected presentations. {ledger.remaining_individual_reviews > 0 ? `Another ${ledger.remaining_original_cohort_reviews} original candidates and ${ledger.remaining_additional_cohort_reviews} additional workflow-origin records require individual review.` : 'All screened signal records now have individual classifications. Briefing/research-document review and production acceptance remain open.'} All {ledger.records.length} current-feed exclusions remain.</p>
    <p>Classification is not a fresh external-source check or independent approval. Historical publication states and indexed URLs remain preserved. A source edit invalidates its pinned classification input and requires re-review before regeneration.</p>
    <p><a href="/data/editorial-classification.json">Download every disposition, original title, source hash and review state</a></p>
    <h2>Why the Amtrak headline changed</h2>
    <p><a href="/signals/57n-amtrak-24-accepted-label-conformance-tests/">FTFN adapter passes 24 Amtrak-label conformance tests</a>. The original title incorrectly attributed internal test passage to Amtrak. The body reported zero real candidate packets or reviewer receipts.</p>
    <h2>Classification archive</h2>
    <p>This is an intentional archive of records excluded from the external-development feed. "Under review" titles quote an unadjudicated historical presentation, not a verified finding. Use the classification filter to distinguish reviewed method notes, research dockets and unresolved records. Review dates are not external observation dates.</p>
    <p>A research docket can combine historical method work with real, separately dated source reviews. The <a href="/signals/57y-preserved-la-starlink-adoption/">Starlink adoption docket</a> preserves its September 1 and September 8 decisions; classification does not turn those receipts into fixtures or establish observed adoption.</p>
    <PagedShelf records={classification} kind="classification" headingLevel={3}/>
  </section>
  <section class="page-section">
    <h2>Measured-outcomes pilot review</h2>
    <p>The measurement feature remains held: no series is admitted. These findings identify missing evidence, not project success or failure. This is not an owner-approved scope reduction or a full-v1 pass.</p>
    {operations.pilot_reviews.map(p=>{const latest=operations.pilot_research_followups.filter(r=>r.pilot_id===p.pilot_id&&r.checked_date<=operations.as_of_date).at(-1);return <article class="record-card"><h3>{p.title}</h3>{latest&&<div data-pilot-latest={latest.review_id}><p>{latest.status} · {latest.checked_date}</p><p>{latest.finding}</p><p><strong>Next:</strong> {latest.next_action}</p><a href={`#${latest.review_id}`}>Exact dated findings and missing artifacts</a></div>}<details><summary>Preserved first-pass extraction · {p.reviewed_date}</summary><p>{p.outcome}</p><p>{p.finding}</p><p><strong>Next at that review:</strong> {p.next_action}</p><p><a href={p.artifact_url}>Exact candidate artifact</a></p></details></article>})}
    <p><a href="/data/current-operations.json">Inspect extraction candidates, period conflicts and review limits</a></p>
  </section>
  <section class="page-section">
    <h2>Evidence backlog: 25 AI determinations completed</h2>
    <p>{operations.backlog_research_checked} retained research receipts have {operations.backlog_authorized_dispositions} owner-authorized determinations: {adjudications.backlog.filter(d=>d.disposition==='Qualify').length} qualified uses and {adjudications.backlog.filter(d=>d.disposition==='Reject inference').length} rejected inferences. No record in this batch awaits human adjudication. These decisions do not admit a measured series or authorize publication.</p>
    <ul>{operations.backlog_reviews.map(r => {const d=adjudications.backlog.find(d=>d.backlog_item_id===r.backlog_item_id)!;return <li><a href={`${r.route}#${r.review_id}`}>{r.title}</a> — <strong>{d.disposition}</strong>. {d.rationale}</li>;})}</ul>
    <p>Historical source dates remain unchanged. Retrieval failures and incomplete table extraction are documented limits, not absence findings. The dated evidence-cycle gates remain separate.</p>
    <p><a href="/data/current-operations.json">Download the individual research receipts and exact artifact locations</a></p>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
